<title>UK: Heathrow still dominates BAA cargo data.</title>
<headline>Heathrow still dominates BAA cargo data.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Heathrow continues to dominate BAA cargo statistics with London's third airport at Stansted making the sharpest growth, latest BAA statistics show.</p>
<p>Cargo handled by BAAs seven UK airports rose by 6.5 percent in May to 131,031 tonnes with Heathrow scoring a 7.4 percent gain whilst cargo at the much smaller Stansted airport grew by 23.2 percent.</p>
<p>This reflects British Airways' decision because of pressure on landing and take-off slots to shift cargo to Stansted from Gatwick where cargo handled dropped in May.</p>
